  "question": {
    "text": "A man is walking on a straight line. The arithmetic mean of the reciprocals of the intercepts of this line on the coordinate axes is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Three stones <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> are placed at the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> respectively. Then which of these stones is<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>/</mo></math>are on the path of the man?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KXZly",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> only",
